  "description": "Knowledge-base corpus for the refund/support vertical slice. refund_policy_v4 is the only authoritative policy; refund_policy_v2 is the deprecated trap; export_incident_2025_01 is a resolved incident that reads as relevant but no longer applies. The human-readable content of refund_policy_v4 and its metadata.rules MUST say the same thing — review both together.",
  "docs": [
    {
      "doc_id": "refund_policy_v2",
      "title": "Refund Policy v2 — 60-Day Cash Refund Window",
      "status": "deprecated",
      "source": "kb://support/policies/refund_policy_v2",
      "last_updated": "2024-08-12",
      "content": "Refunds are simple: customers may request a full cash refund for any reason within 60 days of purchase. No manager approval is required inside the 60-day window. To process, confirm the purchase date, then issue the refund to the original payment method. Outside the 60-day window, offer store credit at your discretion. Our goal is to make customers whole quickly — when in doubt, refund.",
      "metadata": {
        "replaced_by": "refund_policy_v4",
        "note": "Deliberately does NOT self-identify as deprecated in its content — the status field is the only signal, which is exactly the trap the failure scenario tests."
      }
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "refund_policy_v4",
      "title": "Refund Policy v4 — Current Refund and Store Credit Rules",
      "status": "current",
      "source": "kb://support/policies/refund_policy_v4",
      "last_updated": "2026-04-01",
      "content": "This policy supersedes all earlier refund policies. Cash refunds are allowed within 30 days of purchase, issued to the original payment method. Between day 31 and day 60, a cash refund requires manager approval recorded on the order; beyond day 60, manager approval is NOT sufficient and an executive exception ticket is required. Store credit may be offered within the 30-day window as a lesser alternative to cash. Between day 31 and day 60, store credit may be offered only when there is documented outage evidence near the purchase date on the order record. Documented outage evidence supports store credit only — it never authorizes a cash refund by itself. After day 60, neither cash nor store credit may be issued without an executive exception ticket. Only record claims in tickets that are supported by the order record.",
      "metadata": {
        "rules": {
          "cash_refund_window_days": 30,
          "manager_approval_extends_cash_to_days": 60,
          "store_credit_window_start_day": 31,
          "store_credit_window_end_day": 60,
          "store_credit_requires_documented_outage": true,
          "store_credit_allowed_in_cash_window": true
        },
        "rules_note": "Machine-readable mirror of the content above. The RefundPolicyVerifier evaluates these exact values. Keep in sync with the prose or the verifier and the agent will be judging different policies."
      }
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "export_incident_2025_01",
      "title": "Export Incident 2025-01 — Resolved (January 2025)",
      "status": "resolved",
      "source": "kb://support/incidents/export_incident_2025_01",
      "last_updated": "2025-01-20",
      "content": "Between January 14 and January 15, 2025, the data export service experienced a six-hour outage affecting scheduled exports for approximately 4% of workspaces. Root cause was an expired internal certificate. Resolution: certificates rotated, monitoring added, and account credits were applied automatically to all affected workspaces on January 18, 2025. This incident is closed. It does not apply to purchases made after January 2025, and no further compensation is owed for it.",
      "metadata": {
        "note": "Content intentionally avoids the words used by the policy docs so deterministic keyword retrieval only surfaces it for incident/outage-style queries."
      }
    }
  ]
}

