    "summary": "The optional-step-to-list conversion is hand-rolled eight times in one file, in two different spellings: `[s for s in [refund.issued_at_step] if s is not None]` at lines 183/189/210/234/270/275 and `[x] if x is not None else []` at lines 451/475, instead of one tiny `_step_list(step: int | None) -> list[int]` helper.",
    "failure_scenario": "Eight call sites must be found and edited in lockstep whenever step-id handling changes (dedup, multiple provenance steps, making steps required); the two spellings already prove the convention drifts, and a missed site silently emits FailedChecks/EvidenceItems whose step_ids disagree with the rest of the verifier, breaking dashboard step linking and the pinned-expectation tests."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/trace_harness/cli.py",
    "line": 140,
    "summary": "_verify, _attribute, and _bundle each re-implement the same read-artifacts boilerplate — `ArtifactStore.for_run_path(run_dir)` + `TaskSpec.model_validate(store.read_json(run_id, names.TASK_SPEC))` (3 copies) + `store.read_trace(run_id)` (3 copies) + `VerifierResult.model_validate(store.read_json(...))` and the passed-guard (2 copies) — instead of one shared `_load_run_context()` helper or a typed `ArtifactStore.read_model(run_id, name, model_cls)`.",
    "failure_scenario": "Any change to artifact parsing (schema_version check, migration shim, friendlier validation errors) must be replicated into three commands; a missed copy means `bundle` crashes or misreads an artifact that `verify` accepted on the same run dir, and the trio drifts every time a new field load is added to one stage."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/trace_harness/models/fixture.py",
    "line": 74,
    "summary": "FixtureModelAdapter.from_file re-implements the load-JSON-then-model_validate-with-path-in-error pattern that tasks/loader.py already centralizes in `_read_json` + `load_task` (its docstring even claims to be 'the single place where JSON becomes validated Pydantic objects'), with a different error shape that mashes JSONDecodeError and ValidationError into one message.",
    "failure_scenario": "The two loaders' error UX has already diverged (loader: 'invalid task spec in {path}:\\n{exc}' with readable multi-line pydantic output; fixture: one-line 'invalid fixture script {path}: {exc}'), so a fix to fixture-authoring diagnostics, encoding handling, or missing-file messaging in loader.py never reaches script loading, and the CLI prints two different error styles for the same class of authoring mistake."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/trace_harness/attribution/heuristic.py",
